course: dictionary
lesson: 14554
title: Philosophical
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them help you choose the right one. «Philosophical» has two main meanings, and the sentence tells you which one is needed.
explain: «The class had a philosophical discussion about whether it is fair to share everything equally.» Here it means to do with deep thinking about big questions like what is true, right or real. Ask yourself: is the sentence about thinking deeply? It is, so this is the first meaning.
explain: «When his team lost the final, Sam was philosophical and said, "There is always next year."» Here it means calm and accepting when something bad happens. Ask yourself: does Sam stay calm about the loss? He does, so this is the second meaning.
fact: «Philosophical» is an adjective. The noun is philosophy and the adverb is philosophically.
fact: «Philosophical» can mean thinking deeply about big questions, such as what is true, right or real.
fact: «Philosophical» can also mean calm and accepting when something bad happens.
fact: Be philosophical about something means to accept it calmly, without making a fuss.
fact: Philosophy for children (P4C) is a way of learning where pupils ask and discuss big questions together.
exercise: «The class had a philosophical discussion about what is fair.» What does philosophical mean here? | Written in a short poem | Very loud and noisy | Happy to be on holiday | *To do with deep thinking about big questions
exercise: «Mia was philosophical when her kite got stuck in the tree.» What does philosophical suggest? | Sleepy | *Calm and accepting | Angry and shouting | Frightened of trees
exercise: Which question would be a philosophical question? | What time is lunch? | How many legs does a spider have? | *Is it ever right to lie? | Where did I put my pencil case?
test: In P4C, the class asked, «Is it ever OK to lie?» What kind of question is this? | A maths question with one answer | *A philosophical question about what is right | A question about the weather | A question about where to buy sweets
test: «When the match was rained off, Ben was philosophical and said, "Never mind, we will play next week."» What does philosophical mean here? | Hungry | *Calm and accepting | Angry and loud | Confused about the rules
exam: Which means being calm about bad news? | Running away from home | Shouting at everyone | *Accepting it calmly | Asking for a second chance
